Speech-recognition and speaker-diarization model weights downloaded on demand
by Speedwave's meeting-transcription feature. These files are NOT bundled in
the installer — they are fetched (with SHA-256 verification) from the upstream
hosts listed below the first time the user enables a model, and stored under
`~/.speedwave/models/`.

--- Whisper speech-to-text weights (ggml format) ---

OpenAI Whisper model weights, repackaged in whisper.cpp's `ggml` format.

Upstream: https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp
Original model: https://github.com/openai/whisper
License: MIT (OpenAI's Whisper models are released under the MIT license; the
ggml repackaging adds no additional restrictions).

--- Speaker-diarization models (ONNX) ---

The diarization pipeline uses two ONNX models published by k2-fsa as
"sherpa-onnx pretrained models":

  * a speaker-segmentation model derived from pyannote/segmentation-3.0
  * a speaker-embedding model derived from NVIDIA NeMo's TitaNet

Upstream: https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases (speaker-segmentation
and speaker-embedding archives)
Underlying model licenses:
  * pyannote segmentation: MIT
  * NeMo TitaNet embedding: CC-BY-4.0 (NVIDIA NeMo model card)

Speedwave only downloads and runs these weights locally; it does not
redistribute them. If you redistribute a copy of `~/.speedwave/models/`, the
above licenses apply to the respective files.
